&lt;h2&gt;And so…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Nintendo Switch browser scored 339 out of 555 potential points. Not bad
for browsing but it certainly isn&amp;#39;t equipped for game development. Lack of
support for WebGL, WebM, the Web Animations API, and IndexedDB certainly
inhibits the kinds of games you could make, so this might explain their
silence on the NWF front.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oh well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a Switch and want to see these results for yourself, here are the
steps needed to access the web browser:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go to &lt;code&gt;System Settings&lt;/code&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;Internet&lt;/code&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;Internet Settings&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select the network you want to join or are already connected to&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;code&gt;Change Settings&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;code&gt;DNS Settings&lt;/code&gt; and choose &lt;code&gt;Manual&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Under &lt;code&gt;DNS Settings&lt;/code&gt;, select &lt;code&gt;Primary DNS&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replace the contents with &lt;code&gt;045.055.142.122&lt;/code&gt; and hit &lt;code&gt;OK&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Save!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect to the network you just modified DNS settings for, and you should
see a message saying &amp;quot;Registration is required to use this network&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proceed and you&amp;#39;ll be redirected to Google, where you can search for
DuckDuckGo and use that search engine instead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Extra stuff&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The useragent Nintendo is going with is &lt;code&gt;Mozilla/5.0 (Nintendo Switch; WifiWebAuthApplet) AppleWebKit/601.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) NF/4.0.0.7.9 NintendoBrowser/5.1.0.15785&lt;/code&gt;. I am SO glad their useragent isn&amp;#39;t the usual
fugly spaghetti soup that most browsers come up with. The screen size is 1280
by 720.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I remember when people made websites for the Nintendo DS, back when the
browser (made by Opera) came in a &lt;em&gt;cartridge&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.nintendo.co.jp/ds/browser/index.html"&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. I still have mine btw. It
also came with RAM (&amp;quot;Memory Expansion Pak&amp;quot;) you put in the GBA slot for a
whopping 8MB. IGN gave it a 3.5 out of 10. HAHAHAHAHAHA&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good times. 🕸&lt;/p&gt;
